    "Operation": "Provoz",
    "Optional local wind sensor, for example sensor.netatmo_tuuli_ms using m/s. Valid readings are averaged over the last 30 minutes. ThermalPilot learns a separate wind effect only after enough varied observations; no fixed wind penalty is assumed. Missing, invalid or unchanged-for-two-hours readings are ignored, and normal temperature-based planning and heating continue. Fresh wind correction gradually returns to typical conditions in forecasts further ahead. A stable calm reading may also be ignored conservatively. Units are detected automatically.": "Volitelný vítr, automatické jednotky, průměr 30 min. Efekt učený z různých dat. Chybějící, neplatný či 2 h stálý ignorován; topení pokračuje. Dálková předpověď jde k běžnému větru.",
    "Optional price forecast unavailable; planning uses confirmed prices and the normal heat reserve.": "Předpověď chybí; potvrzené ceny a běžná zásoba.",
    "Optional sensor with forecast timestamp/value entries, such as Nordpool Predict FI. Only relative expensive/cheap patterns after confirmed prices are used, so no forecast price unit or additional costs are required. The Source price unit setting applies only to the confirmed total-price sensor. An expensive upcoming period can increase the heat reserve at the end of the known-price plan. Forecast prices are not compared directly with your total prices, used as confirmed prices or used to execute future heating commands. Missing forecasts keep normal planning. Confirmed prices always determine the executable schedule.": "Volitelný relativní trend po potvrzených cenách. Jednotky a přirážky netřeba. Může zvýšit zásobu, nikdy potvrzená cena či přímý budoucí příkaz. Chybí: běžný plán.",
