    "Select the measured supply-water temperature. A temperature sensor uses its state; a climate entity uses its current_temperature attribute. This is the measured water temperature, not the thermostat’s target. Optional for water-based systems. A valid reading adjusts the estimated heating output. Without it, planning and learning continue from observed thermostat demand, without a water-temperature adjustment. Missing readings do not force fallback targets.": "Volitelná měřená přívodní voda; climate používá current_temperature, ne cíl. Koriguje výkon. Chybění nezastaví učení/plán ani nevynutí zálohu.",
